🔹 What is pipe_fd?
pipe_fd is an array of 2 integers. It is used to store two file descriptors returned by the pipe() system call.

int pipe_fd[2];


pipe(pipe_fd);



it fills pipe_fd[0] and pipe_fd[1] with the file descriptors for the read and write ends of the pipe.
"fd" stands for File Descriptor.



A file descriptor is an integer that the OS uses to refer to an open file, device, or communication channel (like a pipe).
